    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d992">

                <pb facs="1034" n="1022" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1022"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7490F/5–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-24T16:00:00+03:06">May 24, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 26—3:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. ReDept 136 Apr [<hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>] 17 to London [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jidda</hi>].<anchor n="20" xml:id="d992-f1"/> Saudi Govt
                    informs me they consider that they have already reserved all rights of <pb
                        facs="1035" n="1023" xml:id="pg1023"/> modification of contract at any time
                    in future by virtue of their notice given Nov 21, 1944. They have today so
                    officially notified British Govt and Cable and Wireless Co.</p>
                <p>I am transmitting proposal in Depts No. 145, May 22, regarding which, however,
                    Saudi Govt assures me June 1 date is of no consequence as they are certain of
                    their freedom to establish any external communications they wish.</p>
                <p>Rptd London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d992-f1" n="20" xml:id="d992-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 3898 to London, <ref target="#pg1021">p. 1021</ref>.</p>
            </note>
